## Architecture rules

A request flows through the same layers every time; each layer talks only to the next one:

```text
{{ fw }} page (useForm / router / Link) → routes/web.php → controller → form request → service → model → {{ dbname }}
controller → Inertia::render('Page', props from resources) → page props;  write → redirect + Inertia::flash() → page.flash
```

- **Routes** (`routes/web.php`) map URLs to controller actions and name them (`notes.index`). Simple static pages may use `Route::inertia('/about', 'About')`.
- **Controllers** are thin: take a form request, call one service method, return `Inertia::render()` for pages or a redirect after writes (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE never render; they redirect, and Inertia follows). No queries, no business rules.
- **Form requests** (`app/Http/Requests`) hold validation rules and typed accessors (`$request->title()`). Failed validation redirects back with errors; the page shows them from `form.errors`. Laravel trims strings and turns empty strings into `null` before validation.
- **Services** (`app/Services`) hold business rules and all queries of a feature. They receive plain values or models and return models or collections; no HTTP objects, no Inertia.
- **Models** (`app/Models`) describe persistence: fillable attributes (`#[Fillable]`), casts, relations and scopes. Document columns with `@property` so Larastan knows their types.
- **Resources** (`app/Http/Resources`) turn models into page props (`NoteResource::collection($notes)->resolve()`). Never pass models to pages directly: every attribute would reach the browser. Keep each resource in sync with its TypeScript type in `resources/js/types/index.ts`.
- **Pages** (`resources/js/Pages`) receive typed props, write through `useForm` (forms) or `router` (e.g. delete), and navigate with `Link`. No `fetch`/axios for page data. Page titles come from `<Head title="…" />`; `{{ entry }}` appends the app name.
- **Components** (`resources/js/Components`) are presentational: {% if vue %}props in, events out (`defineProps`, `defineEmits`){% else %}props in, callbacks out{% endif %}; no `router` or `useForm` inside unless the component is a form (like `NoteForm`).
- **Shared props and flash:** `HandleInertiaRequests::share()` adds props to every page (the app name); `Inertia::flash('success', '…')` shows a one-time message in `AppLayout`. Declare both in `resources/js/types/inertia.d.ts`.
- **Errors:** validation errors come back as `errors` props (per field); missing models return 404 through route model binding (`Note $note`); other exceptions are logged and shown as Laravel's error page (details only when `APP_DEBUG=true`).

