## Configuration and environment

- One `.env` in the project root; `.env.example` lists every key with a comment and is committed. Never commit `.env` or print secret values (`APP_KEY`, passwords).
- The app name comes **only** from `APP_NAME`: `config('app.name')` → the shared prop `appName` → the header and page titles. Never hardcode it in PHP, Blade or {{ fw }}.
- Only `config/*.php` calls `env()`; everywhere else use `config('file.key')` (Larastan enforces it, and `php artisan optimize` caches config in production). To add a setting: add the key to `.env.example` and `.env`, read it in a config file (`'key' => env('MY_KEY', 'default')`), use `config('…')`, and document it in `README.md`.
- The browser receives what pages get as props, plus `VITE_*` keys that Vite compiles into the bundle at build time (`VITE_APP_NAME`; the pages use the shared prop `appName` instead{% if choices.docker != "none" %}, which also works in the Docker image built without `.env`{% endif %}). Vite expands `$VAR` in `.env` values even inside single quotes, so a `VITE_*` copy of a value with `$` differs from what Laravel reads (literally). Never put secrets into props or `VITE_*` keys.
- Ports: `APP_PORT` ({{ ports.APP_PORT }}) for the app (keep `APP_URL` on the same port), `VITE_PORT` ({{ ports.VITE_PORT }}) for Vite.
{%- if choices.database == "sqlite" %}
- Database: `DB_DATABASE=data/database.sqlite`, relative to the project root; `php artisan migrate` creates the file.
{%- elif choices.docker == "none" %}
- Database: {{ dbname }} runs on this machine; create the database and set `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_DATABASE`, `DB_USERNAME`, `DB_PASSWORD` in `.env`, then run `php artisan migrate`.
{%- else %}
- Database: the `db` container creates the database and user from `DB_DATABASE`, `DB_USERNAME`, `DB_PASSWORD` on its first start (changing them later requires a new data volume). {% if full %}PHP runs in containers, so `.env` points at `db:{% if choices.database == "postgres" %}5432{% else %}3306{% endif %}`; database tools on this machine connect to 127.0.0.1:`FORWARD_DB_PORT` ({{ ports.FORWARD_DB_PORT }}).{% else %}`.env` points PHP on this machine at the published port 127.0.0.1:`FORWARD_DB_PORT` ({{ ports.FORWARD_DB_PORT }}); the `app` container overrides it with `db:{% if choices.database == "postgres" %}5432{% else %}3306{% endif %}` in `docker-compose.yml`.{% endif %}
{%- endif %}
- `php artisan serve` restarts when `.env` changes; Vite reads `.env` at start.

## How to

### Add a page

1. Create `resources/js/Pages/<Name>.{{ ext }}` (subfolders become part of the name: `Pages/Tasks/Index.{{ ext }}` is `Tasks/Index`). Set the title with `<Head title="…" />`.
2. Add a route: `Route::inertia('/about', 'About')` for a static page, or a controller action that returns `Inertia::render('<Name>', [...props])`.
3. Declare the props: {% if vue %}`defineProps<{ … }>()`{% else %}a props type on the component function{% endif %}, with shared types in `resources/js/types/index.ts`.
4. Link to it with `Link` (and add it to the navigation in `resources/js/Layouts/AppLayout.{{ ext }}` when it is a main page).
5. Add a feature test that asserts the component and props (`assertInertia`).

### Add a feature (example: tasks)

1. `{{ run }}php artisan make:model Task -mf` → model, migration, factory. Write the migration (below), `#[Fillable]` and `@property` docs on the model, and the factory `definition()`.
2. `app/Services/TaskService.php`: queries and business rules (constructor injection wherever it is used).
3. `{{ run }}php artisan make:request StoreTaskRequest`: `authorize()` returns `true` (or a real check), `rules()`, typed accessors.
4. `{{ run }}php artisan make:resource TaskResource`: the fields the pages need, in camelCase; add the matching `Task` type to `resources/js/types/index.ts`.
5. `{{ run }}php artisan make:controller TaskController`: inject the service; actions return `Inertia::render('Tasks/Index', ['tasks' => TaskResource::collection(...)->resolve()])` or `to_route('tasks.index')` with `Inertia::flash()`.
6. Routes in `routes/web.php`, named `tasks.index`, `tasks.store`… Use route model binding (`{task}` → `Task $task`).
7. Page `resources/js/Pages/Tasks/Index.{{ ext }}` and components in `resources/js/Components/`; a navigation link in `AppLayout.{{ ext }}`.
8. `tests/Feature/TasksTest.php`: list (`assertInertia`), create (valid and invalid input), delete, 404s.

The Notes feature is the reference for every layer: `routes/web.php`, `NoteController`, `StoreNoteRequest`, `NoteService`, `Note`, `NoteResource`, the notes migration and factory, `Pages/Notes/Index.{{ ext }}`, `Components/NoteForm.{{ ext }}`, `Components/NoteCard.{{ ext }}`, `tests/Feature/NotesTest.php`. When it is no longer useful, remove all of these, the navigation link, and add a migration that drops the `notes` table.

### Add a migration

- `{{ run }}php artisan make:migration add_due_date_to_tasks_table`; write `up()` and `down()`, then `{{ run }}php artisan migrate`.
- Never edit a migration that may have run anywhere (another machine, production); add a new one.
- Use the schema builder only (no raw SQL), so migrations run on {% if choices.database == "sqlite" %}any database{% else %}{{ dbname }} and on the SQLite database of the tests{% endif %}. Add indexes for columns you filter or sort by, and `constrained()->cascadeOnDelete()` (or `nullOnDelete()`) for relations.
{%- if choices.docker != "none" %}
- The production container applies pending migrations on start (`docker/entrypoint.sh`).
{%- endif %}

### Add shared data (every page)

Add the prop in `HandleInertiaRequests::share()` (keep it small, it is sent with every response; use a closure for values that need a query), declare its type in `sharedPageProps` in `resources/js/types/inertia.d.ts`, and read it with `usePage().props`.

## Testing

- `{{ run }}composer test` runs PHPUnit with `phpunit.xml`: `APP_ENV=testing` and an in-memory SQLite database (forced, so tests never touch the real database).
- **Feature tests** (`tests/Feature`) call routes: `$this->get('/notes')->assertInertia(fn (Assert $page) => $page->component('Notes/Index')->has('notes', 2))`; writes with `$this->post(...)->assertRedirect(...)->assertSessionHasErrors(...)`, `assertInertiaFlash()`, `assertDatabaseHas()`. Use `RefreshDatabase` and model factories. `assertInertia` also checks that the page component file exists.
- **Unit tests** (`tests/Unit`) cover single classes (resources, services with mocked dependencies).
- `Tests\TestCase` disables Vite, so tests need no build and no dev server.
- Every new route, rule or bug fix gets a test.{% if choices.database != "sqlite" %} Behaviour specific to {{ dbname }} (JSON columns, full-text search, locking) is not covered by the SQLite tests: check it against the real database by hand.{% endif %}

## Definition of done

1. `{{ run }}composer check` passes with **zero** errors and warnings (Pint, Larastan at level max, PHPUnit, ESLint with `--max-warnings=0`, Prettier, `{% if vue %}vue-tsc{% else %}tsc{% endif %}`).
2. `{{ run }}npm run build` succeeds{% if choices.docker != "none" %}, and `docker compose build app` still builds the production image when `Dockerfile`, dependencies or runtime files changed{% endif %}.
3. New behaviour is covered by tests; the page works in the browser (`{% if full %}docker compose up dev{% else %}composer dev{% endif %}`).
4. Docs match the code: `.env.example`, `README.md`{% if options.spec_md %}, `SPEC.md`{% endif %} and this file are updated when commands, env keys, structure or rules change.

## Conventions

- PHP: types on every parameter, return value and property; constructor injection instead of facades in services and controllers (except `Inertia`, `DB`, `Log`); generics in PHPDoc for collections (`Collection<int, Note>`). Never silence Larastan with `@phpstan-ignore` without a comment that explains why.
- TypeScript: strict; no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no non-null assertions (`!`); narrow instead. Import project files through the `@/` alias (`@/Components/NoteCard{% if vue %}.vue{% endif %}`); type-only imports use `import type`.
- Naming: controllers `<Model>Controller`, requests `Store<Model>Request` / `Update<Model>Request`, services `<Model>Service`, resources `<Model>Resource`; pages `Pages/<Plural>/Index|Show|Edit.{{ ext }}`; components `PascalCase.{{ ext }}`; routes `<plural>.<action>`; database `snake_case`, props and TypeScript `camelCase`.
- Styling: {% if choices.css == "tailwind" %}Tailwind utilities in markup for one-off layout; repeated building blocks as component classes in `resources/css/app.css` (`@apply`); dark mode with `dark:` variants (follows the OS).{% elif choices.css == "bootstrap" %}Bootstrap components and utility classes in markup; only app-specific layout goes into `resources/css/app.css`, using Bootstrap's CSS variables (`var(--bs-…)`). A dark theme is `data-bs-theme="dark"` on `<html>` (Bootstrap color modes).{% else %}semantic class names in markup, styles in `resources/css/app.css` using the CSS variables defined at the top; dark mode through the `prefers-color-scheme` block.{% endif %}
- Let the formatters format (`{{ run }}composer format`); do not hand-format or disable lint rules to get green.
- Dependencies: prefer Laravel's own features and existing packages; add a package only when it clearly pays off, and commit the lockfile.
- Write code, comments, UI texts and docs in English.
