## Docker
{% if full %}
Mode: **everything in Docker**. `docker-compose.yml` has these services:

- `dev` (profile `dev`, stage `dev` of `Dockerfile`: PHP 8.5, Composer, Node.js 24, user `app`): mounts the project at `/app`, keeps `vendor/` and `node_modules/` in named volumes, publishes `APP_PORT` and `VITE_PORT`. `docker compose up dev` runs the servers of `npm run dev:all` (what `composer dev` runs; keep the `CMD` of the `dev` stage in sync); `docker compose run --rm dev <command>` runs anything else. It does not load `.env` as environment: Laravel and Vite read the file themselves (`php artisan serve` even drops other variables for the PHP server), so settings belong in `.env`; the `environment:` entries only make the servers listen on `0.0.0.0`.
- `app`: the production image, `docker compose up --build app`.
{%- if choices.database != "sqlite" %}
- `db`: {{ dbname }} with a health check; `dev` and `app` wait for it.
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
Mode: **Docker to run the app**. Development happens on this machine (`composer dev`); Docker builds and runs the production image{% if choices.database != "sqlite" %} and the {{ dbname }} server (`db`), which `composer dev` needs: the Dev command starts it with `docker compose up -d --wait db`{% endif %}.
{%- endif %}

- `Dockerfile` (multi-stage): Composer installs production dependencies, Node.js builds `public/build`, and the runtime stage (`dunglas/frankenphp`, PHP 8.5 with `pdo_sqlite`, `pdo_pgsql`, `pdo_mysql`) serves `public/` on port 8080 as user `app`. `docker/entrypoint.sh` runs `php artisan optimize` and `migrate --force` on every start. `.env` is never copied into images; the `app` service gets it through `env_file`, with `APP_ENV=production` and `APP_DEBUG=false`.
- **Data:** `DOCKER_DATA` in `.env` decides where containers keep {% if choices.database == "sqlite" %}the SQLite database (`/app/data`){% else %}the {{ dbname }} data{% endif %}: {% if choices.data == "local" %}**`./data`** — the project's `data/` folder (current setting); set `DOCKER_DATA=data` to use a Docker volume instead.{% else %}**`data`** — the named volume `{{ project.slug }}_data` (current setting); `docker compose down -v` deletes it. Set `DOCKER_DATA=./data` to keep the files in the project's `data/` folder instead.{% endif %}
- Everything is named after `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` ({{ project.slug }}). Stop with `docker compose{% if full %} --profile dev{% endif %} down` (add `-v` to delete the volumes).
- When the app needs another PHP extension, add it to `install-php-extensions` in the `base` stage{% if full %} and rebuild (`docker compose build dev app`){% endif %}.
{%- endif %}

